      \(e^{c(s-1/2)^2}\), with \(c=1.980100780386\ldots\), cancels the single dyadic curvature
      algebraically but raises the completed function from order one to order two. Every zero-free entire
      order-one factor is \(e^{a+bs}\) and has zero logarithmic curvature. An order-one factor with nonzero
