    <p>It is independent of height and vanishes exactly on the critical line. A displacement \(1/4\) retains
      the value \(0.881373587020\ldots\) at every ordinate. This solves seam accounting and coercive detection,
      not seam control: symmetric off-real zeros are compatible with a Blaschke product, and no current prime
      or theta estimate forces the supremum marker to zero. Full details are in
