<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Dual prime-error attempt</p>
    <h2 id="t-rh-dual-prime-error-routes">Did either remaining prime-error route close the proof?</h2>
    <p>No. The square-root Chebyshev route and the uniform signed-Laguerre route reach the same analytic
      boundary. Under \(z=(s-2)/(s+1)\), the unit disk is exactly \(\Re s&gt;1/2\).</p>
    <p>If prime error were controlled only at exponent \(\theta\ge1/2\), the corresponding centered disk and
      coefficient base would be</p>
    <p class="formula">\[
